1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,730
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:31,072
<i>One million for Madrigal's body.</i>

6
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>And another million for Diego's corpse.</i>

7
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:36,703
[Ivy] <i>Okay. We can't afford</i>
<i>to make any more mistakes.</i>

8
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:40,040
<i>I need a strong case against Emilia.</i>

9
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,875
[Georgina] <i>We need a whistleblower.</i>
<i>Divine Uytengco.</i>

10
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:43,334
[Julio] <i>I will make sure</i>

11
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:46,629
<i>our kingdom is still standing</i>
<i>when you wake up.</i>

12
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:52,343
<i>I will go against Diego Torillo.</i>
<i>I will run for governor.</i>

13
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:54,471
<i>My conscience keeps eating at me.</i>

14
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:57,348
<i>I'm ready to divulge</i>
<i>Ma'am Emilia's corrupt activities.</i>

15
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:59,517
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy and Diego's lives</i>
<i>are in danger.</i>

16
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:02,020
<i>Julio has issued a shoot-to-kill</i>
<i>order against them.</i>

17
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:03,188
-[screams]
-[Jepoy firing shots]

18
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,064
<i>Get down!</i>

19
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:05,607
[gunshots]

20
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:07,650
[Ivy] <i>What's happening? Mom!</i>

21
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:09,903
<i>You're a monster, Julio Ardiente!</i>

22
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,488
-<i>Camia Cruz!</i>
-[shots fired]

23
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:14,115
[Diego grunting]

24
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:14,991
[Marlon] <i>Diego!</i>

25
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:19,454
[Julio] <i>Make sure Diego Torillo</i>
<i>knows he was the target</i>

26
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:21,039
<i>of the shootout.</i>

27
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:23,333
<i>That way he'll know he's responsible</i>

28
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:24,959
<i>for what happened to his supporters.</i>

29
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:28,087
<i>-Who shot my mother?!</i>
<i>-Julio Ardiente.</i>

30
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:30,131
<i>Julio, you bastard.</i>

31
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:41,226
Doctor, how's my mother doing?

32
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,228
[doctor] She had to undergo surgery, but…

33
00:01:43,311 --> 00:01:44,729
we were able to revive her.

34
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,482
[Anna] Is she safe now?

35
00:01:47,565 --> 00:01:49,776
[doctor] Yes, she's in the
recovery room right now.

36
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:52,737
We'll inform you when you can visit her.

37
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:55,698
All right, doc. Thank you very much.

38
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:05,959
[Loring] That Julio Ardiente
is nothing but a demon!

39
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:09,671
He even has the nerve to run for governor!

40
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:13,341
They're confident

41
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:14,759
because they think

42
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:17,971
the people still support them
despite the things they do.

43
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:20,807
But why did he attack now all of a sudden?

44
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:22,016
The Ardientes know.

45
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:25,854
They already know about what you did.

46
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:30,984
They suspect that
you and Jepoy shot Arnaldo,

47
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:33,528
and they attacked the headquarters

48
00:02:33,611 --> 00:02:35,530
because you were one of their targets.

49
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:57,093
I'm sorry about what I said.

50
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:58,928
I just lost my temper.

51
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,681
I didn't mean any of it.

52
00:03:02,473 --> 00:03:06,436
Cut the sweet talk, Raul.
I've already seen this before.

53
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:08,646
[sighs] Just tell it to me straight.

54
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:09,898
What do you need?

55
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:11,816
Do you need my money?

56
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:13,818
My power?

57
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,153
My body?

58
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:18,072
-Just say it.
-Someone met up with Emilia.

59
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:21,242
Another Jaguar like me.

60
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:23,912
If that's true,

61
00:03:24,621 --> 00:03:25,955
then it can only mean one thing.

62
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,293
The real Jaguar is finally out of prison.

63
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,673
<i>Are you Jaguar?</i>

64
00:03:36,424 --> 00:03:37,342
<i>I am.</i>

65
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:42,013
<i>Your men told me that you're</i>
<i>the one who can help me avenge</i>

66
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:43,514
<i>my father's death.</i>

67
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,517
<i>You see, I have a feeling the Ardientes</i>

68
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:48,645
<i>were behind my father's murder.</i>

69
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,063
<i>I'll help you.</i>

70
00:03:50,521 --> 00:03:52,982
<i>I have my men and my weapons.</i>

71
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:54,567
<i>And I have…</i>

72
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,778
<i>lots of money.</i>

73
00:03:56,861 --> 00:03:58,196
<i>We'll get along, then.</i>

74
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:01,741
<i>And why should I trust you, Jaguar?</i>

75
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,661
<i>Because I want to acquire</i>
<i>the Ardiente gambling dens…</i>

76
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:08,289
along with all their power.

77
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:14,295
<i>I need someone who'll act</i>
<i>as Jaguar while I'm in prison</i>

78
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,506
<i>and manage my men while I'm gone.</i>

79
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,758
<i>I should've killed Julio</i>
<i>when I had the chance.</i>

80
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:21,177
<i>We can help each other, Raul.</i>

81
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:24,806
<i>Help me investigate my dad's death,</i>

82
00:04:24,889 --> 00:04:28,935
<i>and… I'll give you everything you need.</i>

83
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,603
[Raul] <i>I decided to go with your deal.</i>

84
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:33,523
[Natalie] <i>So, who killed my father?</i>

85
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:35,566
<i>Emilia had the senator killed.</i>

86
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:37,694
[Natalie screaming]

87
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:39,570
<i>I'll kill her!</i>

88
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,572
<i>Right now, I'm in control</i>
<i>of the situation.</i>

89
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:44,409
<i>So, I can provide you</i>
<i>with everything you need.</i>

90
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:46,452
<i>But you have to give me what I need too.</i>

91
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,746
<i>I need to be stronger than the Ardientes.</i>

92
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:51,457
<i>You can tell Jaguar</i>

93
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:52,750
<i>that Raul finally agreed.</i>

94
00:04:52,834 --> 00:04:54,585
<i>Don't worry, I will.</i>

95
00:04:59,048 --> 00:05:00,383
Then, just give it up!

96
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:05,179
Give Jaguar's mask and identity
back to him.

97
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:07,181
That's what I would do if I were you.

98
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,559
I can't give him back the mask.

99
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:12,729
Not until I've accomplished all my goals.

100
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:16,607
But first, I need Julio Ardiente's power.

101
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:18,526
Okay.

102
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,111
But…

103
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:24,741
you better hunt him down
before he hunts you down first.

104
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:27,660
I'll be ready for him.

105
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:34,125
I'll die before I hand over Jaguar's mask.

106
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:38,963
[tense music playing]

107
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,052
[exhales]

108
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:05,114
<i>I've told you so many times,</i>
<i>but you still haven't changed.</i>

109
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,949
<i>Brother or not, I'll have you locked up</i>

110
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:09,035
<i>if that's what it takes</i>
<i>to set you straight.</i>

111
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:11,287
<i>Then you're a useless brother,</i>
<i>you bastard!</i>

112
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:16,334
[tense music playing]

113
00:06:42,819 --> 00:06:45,404
[woman] Nurse, please make sure
he lives, please.

114
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,077
[man] Doctor! Over here!

115
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:53,663
[man] Miss!

116
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:55,748
Diego.

117
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:58,459
Look at what they did to my mother.

118
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,920
They're monsters!

119
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:04,215
Why did this have to happen to us?

120
00:07:05,341 --> 00:07:07,885
Why did they have to hurt my mother?

121
00:07:09,262 --> 00:07:10,763
-Dear.
-Yes, Mom?

122
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,764
Dear!

123
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:14,016
It hurts!

124
00:07:27,905 --> 00:07:29,115
Those bastards.

125
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:30,283
-Diego.
-All of them.

126
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:34,162
Stop it, Diego!

127
00:07:34,495 --> 00:07:35,830
I said, stop it!

128
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:38,416
What's happening to you?!

129
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:42,628
Anna, you saw what happened to Aunt Camia.

130
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:45,006
The Ardientes were after me.

131
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:48,134
No one else should've gotten involved.

132
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:51,596
If it's me Julio wants,
they should shoot me, not them!

133
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:53,014
Wait, Diego.

134
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:54,932
I said, wait!

135
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:57,101
Don't stop me, Anna.

136
00:07:57,935 --> 00:07:59,979
I'll go straight
to the Ardientes and face them

137
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:01,314
so no one else gets hurt.

138
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:03,024
They'll kill you, Diego!

139
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,527
And if you die, Lily will be all alone!

140
00:08:07,236 --> 00:08:08,404
You'll leave us all alone!

141
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:12,325
The ones who care about you,
the ones who believe in you!

142
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,328
Don't blame yourself.

143
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:18,789
What the Ardientes did was not your fault!

144
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:22,502
So, don't go, Diego.

145
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:26,047
The people here need you.

146
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:28,508
Lily needs you.

147
00:08:41,312 --> 00:08:42,563
-Ivy.
-Jepoy.

148
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,732
What happened? Did the Ardientes
try to kill you too?

149
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:46,567
They ambushed me too.

150
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:47,652
What about you?

151
00:08:47,985 --> 00:08:49,570
I'm okay. But my mother…

152
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:52,490
and Diego were shot by the Ardientes' men.

153
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,909
The Ardientes attacked the headquarters.

154
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:57,912
Thankfully my mother
and Diego are safe now.

155
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:02,333
Jepoy, you need to be more careful…

156
00:09:03,042 --> 00:09:05,628
because Julio has a
shoot-to-kill order against you.

157
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:09,257
The Ardientes know that
you're the one who shot Arnaldo.

158
00:09:12,301 --> 00:09:13,386
Sorry, Ivy.

159
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:14,887
Where are you going?

160
00:09:15,513 --> 00:09:16,931
To the Ardientes' place.

161
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:18,432
I was the one who shot Arnaldo anyway.

162
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:19,517
No.

163
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,769
-Ivy. Ivy, all this is my fault.
-Stay here.

164
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:23,229
No, it's not!

165
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:25,439
Yes, you did shoot Arnaldo.

166
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:26,941
But you only did it to save my life!

167
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:29,360
I owe you my life, Jepoy.

168
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:31,904
If you go to the Ardientes'
house, they will win.

169
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,781
And, after killing you,

170
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:35,074
who will they kill next?

171
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:36,742
They will also kill us.

172
00:09:38,035 --> 00:09:39,453
You're not going anywhere. Stay here.

173
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:41,706
I know you can't wait
to go after the Ardientes.

174
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:43,416
The same goes for me, Jepoy!

175
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:48,004
But we need to stick to the plan.

176
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:53,509
Julio won't know what hit him.

177
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:03,019
[Diego] Miss Cora.

178
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:07,481
I think it would be
better if you hide for a while.

179
00:10:08,065 --> 00:10:09,525
You're not safe here.

180
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:12,486
We'll just call you when we need you.

181
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:16,449
What's important now is your safety.

182
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:21,829
No matter how much
the Ardientes threaten me,

183
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:23,706
you still have my support.

184
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,417
Thank you.

185
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:28,878
Thank you, Diego.

186
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:32,048
Well, I better go.

187
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,926
Please take care.

188
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:38,763
You too.

189
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:45,686
Anna, if only I'd been more vigilant…

190
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:48,731
then I could've protected Aunt Camia.

191
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:52,735
Diego, you can't save everyone.

192
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:55,279
And it's not your fault.

193
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:58,532
It's enough for you
to teach them to be brave

194
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:00,409
and stand up for themselves.

195
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:13,255
[machine beeping]

196
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:15,174
[footsteps approaching]

197
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:24,141
[instrumental theme music playing]

198
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:47,748
Mom.

199
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:12,815
Mom.

200
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,901
Mom, you're awake.

201
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:18,779
I'm so glad you're okay.

202
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:36,589
Mom, I'm sorry.

203
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:39,717
I'm sorry for…

204
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:44,263
getting you involved in my vengeance

205
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:45,639
against the Ardientes.

206
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:48,184
I know…

207
00:12:48,684 --> 00:12:51,312
I could've just taken you
far away from here

208
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:56,025
and lived a peaceful life instead.

209
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:01,447
But I'm sorry, Mom.

210
00:13:05,034 --> 00:13:06,243
I'm sorry.

211
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:10,706
I'm sorry for choosing
to sacrifice myself.

212
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:16,420
But this isn't just for us, Mom.

213
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:22,510
This is for everyone who's ever
been abused by the Ardientes.

214
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,349
I promise I won't let them
hurt you anymore.

215
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:29,600
I promise.

216
00:13:29,683 --> 00:13:31,810
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]
<i>♪ Let her cry ♪</i>

217
00:13:31,894 --> 00:13:36,190
<i>♪ For she's a lady ♪</i>

218
00:13:36,273 --> 00:13:39,151
<i>♪ Let her dream… ♪</i>

219
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:40,945
I love you so much, Mom.

220
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:45,366
Thank you for always being by my side.

221
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:51,163
[sniffles]

222
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:57,002
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower</i>
<i>Growing wild ♪</i>

223
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,172
[suspenseful music playing]

224
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:02,258
[phone ringing]

225
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,641
Hello?

226
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:12,685
I'll be needing your help again.

227
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:19,316
It's time to take down
Emilia Ardiente next.

228
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:30,494
Hello, darling!

229
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:33,664
<i>I've transferred 20 million</i>
<i>pesos to your account.</i>

230
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:36,166
No more, no less! Woman of my word.

231
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,543
Thank you, Divine.

232
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,753
I know I can always count on you.

233
00:14:40,045 --> 00:14:43,257
Of course. Just keep the money coming in!

234
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,427
[Emilia] <i>Of course! Don't be silly.</i>

235
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:50,055
There's always more where
that came from, you know?

236
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:52,683
[laughs] I'm sure.
I know I can count on you too.

237
00:14:53,142 --> 00:14:55,144
[Divine] Okay! Gotta go! Bye!

238
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:56,770
[tires screeching]

239
00:14:56,854 --> 00:14:58,147
[Divine] Thank you!

240
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,193
[Divine exclaims]
Who are you?! Who are you?!

241
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:06,822
[Divine exclaiming, wailing]

242
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,574
Someone, help me!

243
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:09,909
Help!

244
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:11,785
Help!

245
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:13,996
[cries] Please don't hurt me!

246
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:26,675
What do you plan to do with her?

247
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:30,763
[tense music playing]

248
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:43,400
Yes, Papa?

249
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:45,361
[Julio] It's a good thing
I caught up with you.

250
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:51,617
You have to hear the results
of our little investigation…

251
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:54,745
on the one who shot your son.

252
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,998
You know, we were able to trace

253
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,541
the gun that was used…

254
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:01,502
by the culprit.

255
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:04,213
Do you know who it's registered under?

256
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:07,424
Let me guess.

257
00:16:07,508 --> 00:16:08,550
Ivy Aguas.

258
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:10,010
Nah.

259
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:11,762
No, no.

260
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:13,097
That would be too…

261
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:14,765
predictable.

262
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:17,393
It doesn't suit our story.

263
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:20,729
It's a plot twist
that no one would've expected.

264
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:23,691
Then, who owns it, Papa?

265
00:16:25,484 --> 00:16:27,820
Surprise! Surprise!

266
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:30,614
The gun belongs to me.

267
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:32,908
What?!

268
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,326
How did it happen?

269
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,788
I was asking myself the same question

270
00:16:38,414 --> 00:16:39,915
until I remembered…

271
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:44,503
how that gun was part of my armory…

272
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:49,174
that got raided by Jaguar.

273
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:55,347
Jaguar was the one
who tried to kill your son.

274
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:57,349
[dramatic music]

275
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:05,065
Boss, another Jaguar attacked us

276
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:06,859
and took over one of our gambling dens.

277
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:09,028
He called you a fake.

278
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:11,321
[man] Hold on, I'm confused.

279
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,740
Who's the real Jaguar, anyway?

280
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:13,866
You or him?

281
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:17,327
It doesn't matter who the real Jaguar is.

282
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:20,039
What matters now is your loyalty.

283
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,665
So, either side with me,

284
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:24,251
or that impostor.

285
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,253
Now,

286
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:28,255
whoever's on my side…

287
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,507
can stay here.

288
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:32,509
While those of you who aren't…

289
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,428
can leave.

290
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:41,477
Me, Boss.

291
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,190
I'm on your side.

292
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,198
What's up with you all?

293
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:56,825
Our boss has been helping us
all this time,

294
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,327
and now you doubt him?

295
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:04,666
Like I said, I'm on your side, Boss.

296
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:07,920
We don't know who that other guy is,

297
00:18:08,003 --> 00:18:09,713
so if I were you, I'd choose to stay.

298
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:14,343
[man] Boss, we're on your side.
We won't let you down.

299
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:22,726
[phone ringing]

300
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:28,524
Hello, Jaguar.

301
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:30,776
We have to talk, and this time around…

302
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:32,444
<i>you have no right to refuse.</i>

303
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,113
This is important.

304
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:39,409
[tense music playing]

305
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:48,252
-Emilia.
-You animal!

306
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:51,463
How could you do this to me?!
You betrayed me!

307
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:53,632
Wait, Emilia. What are you talking about?

308
00:18:53,715 --> 00:18:57,261
Don't play dumb with me!
I know you tried to kill my son!

309
00:18:57,761 --> 00:19:00,931
My father traced the gun
that shot Arnaldo,

310
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:03,350
and this is what he found!
Take a look, traitor!

311
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,351
Hold on, Emilia.

312
00:19:04,434 --> 00:19:06,603
So, don't you dare lie to me!
See for yourself!

313
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:10,816
What are you up really to, huh?!

314
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:16,321
I have no ill intentions toward your son

315
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:18,031
because he's not on my blacklist.

316
00:19:18,615 --> 00:19:20,534
That's the gun I gave Madrigal,

317
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:23,871
but I didn't order him to shoot Arnaldo.

318
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:27,249
He probably did that for personal reasons.

319
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:30,002
I bet he wanted revenge on your family.

320
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:31,211
Then, prove it!

321
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,548
Kill Madrigal! Kill him!

322
00:19:35,048 --> 00:19:37,050
I don't have to prove anything to you.

323
00:19:37,885 --> 00:19:40,429
He's your henchman,
so he's your responsibility!

324
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:41,763
Kill him!

325
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:44,933
[tense music playing]

326
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,165
I'm sorry, Jaguar.

327
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:12,336
But Madrigal has to pay
for what he did to my son.

328
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,922
He will definitely pay for this!

329
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:17,007
He will not get away with this!

330
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:27,184
-Papa, I need to talk to you.
-You got one minute.

331
00:20:27,434 --> 00:20:29,811
I've got a pesky kitten to hunt down!

332
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:34,107
Declaring war with Jaguar
is not gonna be good for you!

333
00:20:34,191 --> 00:20:36,693
You'll be wasting time,
resources, and men!

334
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:39,988
He must pay for what he did to Arnaldo!

335
00:20:40,364 --> 00:20:42,908
Papa, if there's anyone
who has to pay, it's not Jaguar.

336
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:46,536
If not the Jaguar…

337
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:48,622
then who?

338
00:20:58,131 --> 00:21:00,926
[upbeat music playing]

339
00:21:22,906 --> 00:21:25,033
-[Jepoy grunts]
-[Natalie exclaims]

340
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:26,201
-Who are you?!
-Madrigal!

341
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:31,498
Sorry, ma'am.

342
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:34,626
[exhales]

343
00:21:42,801 --> 00:21:44,845
Did the Ardientes do that to you?

344
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:17,919
Congressman.

345
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:19,880
Ivy! [giggles]

346
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:22,341
What a surprise! Please. Please, sit down.

347
00:22:22,924 --> 00:22:23,925
Join me.

348
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:25,510
So…

349
00:22:26,344 --> 00:22:27,637
how have you been?

350
00:22:31,099 --> 00:22:32,392
Honestly, Congressman?

351
00:22:33,101 --> 00:22:34,686
I'm upset with you.

352
00:22:35,395 --> 00:22:37,355
Why? What did I do?

353
00:22:38,356 --> 00:22:39,357
[exhales]

354
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:42,694
Why didn't you tell me…

355
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:45,947
that you already
brought Arnaldo back home?

356
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,410
Well, let me apologize. I'm sorry.

357
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:54,539
But I was thinking,
I know you're a busy woman.

358
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:57,709
Besides, I don't want Arnaldo
to be disturbed for now.

359
00:22:57,793 --> 00:23:00,087
Let him have a couple of days to rest

360
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:03,090
before he starts accepting visitors, okay?

361
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,133
You don't want Arnaldo to be disturbed?

362
00:23:05,217 --> 00:23:08,011
Why? I'm not a troublemaker. And for sure,

363
00:23:08,095 --> 00:23:12,057
when Arnaldo wakes up,
he'll be happy to see his "hon".

364
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,476
Do you know who the troublemaker is?

365
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:16,311
Your daughter, Emilia.

366
00:23:16,853 --> 00:23:17,729
[chuckles]

367
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,149
You know, Ivy, you're a bold one.

368
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:27,447
You know very well that
Emilia is going to raise hell…

369
00:23:28,156 --> 00:23:29,950
if ever she finds out you're here.

370
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:32,160
I don't care.

371
00:23:32,744 --> 00:23:36,665
And she has no right to stop me
if I want to visit Arnaldo.

372
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:40,710
Despite all the terrible things
he did to me,

373
00:23:40,794 --> 00:23:42,045
I'm still here for him.

374
00:23:42,462 --> 00:23:48,260
I'm still concerned about him,
and I want to know who shot him.

375
00:23:48,635 --> 00:23:52,848
And I mean, the one who really shot him.

376
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:56,601
You know, you don't have to wait.

377
00:23:57,644 --> 00:24:00,147
Because we now know who did it.

378
00:24:02,607 --> 00:24:03,900
It's Diego, right?

379
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:05,944
It was all over the news.

380
00:24:06,027 --> 00:24:09,072
Your camp opened fire at his headquarters.

381
00:24:10,949 --> 00:24:13,994
No, no, no, no. It wasn't Diego.

382
00:24:14,744 --> 00:24:15,620
Sad to say…

383
00:24:17,289 --> 00:24:19,457
I made a mistake. You know, Miss Aguas,

384
00:24:19,541 --> 00:24:22,711
I'm the kind of a man
who admits his mistakes.

385
00:24:23,670 --> 00:24:27,841
And I admit that
I was wrong to suspect Diego,

386
00:24:27,924 --> 00:24:29,759
much as I hate his guts.

387
00:24:30,927 --> 00:24:32,762
Well, since you admitted your mistake,

388
00:24:32,846 --> 00:24:37,058
I assume you feel guilty for all
the other people you've hurt.

389
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:39,811
Correction, Ivy…

390
00:24:41,313 --> 00:24:42,981
Yes, I admit I made a mistake.

391
00:24:43,940 --> 00:24:45,984
But feel guilty? No.

392
00:24:46,067 --> 00:24:47,068
Why would I?

393
00:24:47,694 --> 00:24:51,865
They deserved every bullet
that flew all over that place!

394
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:55,035
I tell you, Ivy,

395
00:24:55,493 --> 00:24:57,662
you should've seen their eyes.

396
00:24:57,746 --> 00:25:01,166
The fear in them, when death came calling.

397
00:25:03,418 --> 00:25:05,253
It was priceless!

398
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:06,421
[Julio chuckling]

399
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:13,762
Well, whoever your new suspect is…

400
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:15,680
I hope you finally got the right one.

401
00:25:17,474 --> 00:25:20,644
I don't make mistakes
twice in a row, Miss Aguas.

402
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:25,315
And I have solid evidence this time.

403
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,235
I'm certain

404
00:25:29,236 --> 00:25:32,656
it was Madrigal who shot Arnaldo.

405
00:25:33,823 --> 00:25:34,824
And

406
00:25:35,992 --> 00:25:39,079
my men are looking for him,
even as we speak.

407
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:42,582
And I guarantee you…

408
00:25:44,042 --> 00:25:49,422
Madrigal is not getting out of
this situation alive this time.

409
00:25:51,299 --> 00:25:53,385
-So, it's Madrigal?
-Yes.

410
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:55,470
It's Madrigal.

411
00:25:58,765 --> 00:26:01,017
And he is about to die.

412
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:13,154
[Jepoy] <i>What's this for?</i>

413
00:26:13,238 --> 00:26:14,781
[man] <i>If you hadn't warned our boss,</i>

414
00:26:14,864 --> 00:26:16,616
<i>we would've gotten into bigger trouble.</i>

415
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:19,244
[Jepoy] <i>That was nothing, boss.</i>
<i>This is too much.</i>

416
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:23,081
[Raul] <i>What were you doing</i>
<i>at Mayor Arnaldo's wedding?</i>

417
00:26:23,164 --> 00:26:26,001
<i>I was going to kill Arnaldo,</i>
<i>but I didn't get the chance.</i>

418
00:26:26,334 --> 00:26:29,379
<i>I want to make him feel the</i>
<i>torture they made me go through.</i>

419
00:26:29,462 --> 00:26:32,424
<i>-Leave Mayor Arnaldo to me.</i>
<i>-Why, boss?</i>

420
00:26:33,216 --> 00:26:34,592
<i>Are we supposed to protect him?</i>

421
00:26:36,219 --> 00:26:38,221
[Raul] <i>That's the gun I gave Madrigal.</i>

422
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:41,224
<i>But I didn't order him to shoot Arnaldo.</i>

423
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:43,935
<i>He's your henchman,</i>
<i>so he's your responsibility!</i>

424
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:45,270
<i>Kill him!</i>

425
00:26:53,069 --> 00:26:53,987
[phone ringing]

426
00:26:55,947 --> 00:26:57,115
[phone ringing]

427
00:27:00,618 --> 00:27:03,496
[Julio] Now, who's calling you?

428
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:05,123
[phone ringing]

429
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:08,543
[phone ringing]

430
00:27:09,544 --> 00:27:10,628
No one important.

431
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:18,261
You're so amazing, Congressman.

432
00:27:18,345 --> 00:27:21,056
That's why I look up to you!

433
00:27:21,639 --> 00:27:24,517
Because no one can ever escape
the clutches of…

434
00:27:25,060 --> 00:27:26,895
Julio Ardiente.

435
00:27:27,937 --> 00:27:29,272
[Julio and Ivy chuckling]

436
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:31,191
I don't think I'm wrong

437
00:27:31,274 --> 00:27:33,443
in saying you already
have a place in hell…

438
00:27:34,235 --> 00:27:36,780
for anyone who gets
in your way or your family's.

439
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:40,825
Ivy, that's the only way
that you will get two reactions

440
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:42,369
that are very important in life.

441
00:27:43,661 --> 00:27:48,041
To establish fear
and to get their respect.

442
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:50,001
Bang,

443
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:51,086
bang,

444
00:27:51,544 --> 00:27:52,504
bang.

445
00:27:53,004 --> 00:27:55,215
Anyone you don't like? Shoot them down.

446
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:56,508
Kill them.

447
00:27:56,591 --> 00:27:57,634
If they survive…

448
00:27:59,135 --> 00:28:00,303
well,

449
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:02,514
good luck to them in the next lifetime

450
00:28:02,597 --> 00:28:05,100
because if I see them again,
I will shoot them down again,

451
00:28:05,725 --> 00:28:06,726
even there.

452
00:28:08,228 --> 00:28:09,896
Well, I have to go, Congressman.

453
00:28:09,979 --> 00:28:11,898
I think I've overstayed my welcome.

454
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:16,653
Okay. Like I told you,
I know you're a busy woman.

455
00:28:17,112 --> 00:28:18,238
But do be careful.

456
00:28:19,906 --> 00:28:22,575
-You too. Be very careful.
-Thank you.

457
00:28:27,997 --> 00:28:28,790
Ivy?

458
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:31,376
Yes?

459
00:28:31,876 --> 00:28:34,379
Colonel Sanggano here just informed me

460
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:38,550
that they already know
where to find Madrigal.

461
00:28:39,551 --> 00:28:42,053
Exactly pinpointed…

462
00:28:42,846 --> 00:28:44,681
at the very location.

463
00:28:46,516 --> 00:28:48,143
Would you like to join me?

464
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:53,440
Let's go make that bastard suffer.

465
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,445
I like the sound of that, Congressman.

466
00:28:58,945 --> 00:29:00,530
In case you didn't know,

467
00:29:01,072 --> 00:29:03,324
that's one of my favorite activities…

468
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:05,410
getting payback.

469
00:29:06,578 --> 00:29:10,123
A woman after my own heart. My, my!

470
00:29:10,874 --> 00:29:12,876
[tense music playing]

471
00:29:22,552 --> 00:29:23,928
Auntie, I'm sorry.

472
00:29:26,055 --> 00:29:28,224
The Ardientes were there
because they were after me.

473
00:29:29,684 --> 00:29:31,060
But you got caught in the crossfire.

474
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:32,729
Diego.

475
00:29:34,689 --> 00:29:37,817
I've accepted the fact that
I have one foot in the grave.

476
00:29:39,402 --> 00:29:41,905
Like everyone else fighting the Ardientes.

477
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:45,408
What we need to do now…

478
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:48,661
is stay wary.

479
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:51,581
Auntie, I promise you that…

480
00:29:53,041 --> 00:29:54,959
I won't let anyone's life

481
00:29:55,043 --> 00:29:57,587
be taken away for the sake of this fight.

482
00:29:58,838 --> 00:30:00,048
[phone ringing]

483
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:05,720
[Diego] Excuse me.

484
00:30:05,804 --> 00:30:07,138
[ringing continues]

485
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:09,599
Arthur?

486
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:19,150
We're almost there.

487
00:30:27,075 --> 00:30:28,076
Ivy.

488
00:30:29,452 --> 00:30:31,120
[phone ringing]

489
00:30:53,643 --> 00:30:54,519
Madrigal.

490
00:30:55,061 --> 00:30:56,062
Boss?

491
00:30:56,771 --> 00:30:57,856
Come with me.

492
00:30:57,939 --> 00:30:58,940
Where are we going, Boss?

493
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:01,860
Follow us.

494
00:31:07,156 --> 00:31:09,158
[tense music playing]

495
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:46,279
Divine Uytengco?

496
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:48,531
Arthur.

497
00:31:48,823 --> 00:31:50,116
Ivy asked me…

498
00:31:50,742 --> 00:31:51,910
to bring her here.

499
00:31:53,077 --> 00:31:54,203
But she won't talk.

500
00:31:55,288 --> 00:31:57,332
You're better at this.

501
00:31:58,499 --> 00:31:59,667
She might listen to you.

502
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:14,849
[Raul] Did you attempt to
murder Mayor Arnaldo?

503
00:32:14,933 --> 00:32:16,309
I had nothing to do with that, Boss.

504
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:17,769
Why would I do that?

505
00:32:17,852 --> 00:32:19,312
Besides, the Ardientes are our enemies.

506
00:32:19,395 --> 00:32:20,813
We should be celebrating right now.

507
00:32:20,897 --> 00:32:21,981
-We should be drinking--
-[thuds]

508
00:32:23,816 --> 00:32:25,109
Answer me, Madrigal!

509
00:32:25,652 --> 00:32:26,653
Were you involved?

510
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:29,030
Boss…

511
00:32:30,531 --> 00:32:31,282
I'm on your side.

512
00:32:31,366 --> 00:32:33,159
Why are you so concerned
about Arnaldo, anyway?

513
00:32:33,242 --> 00:32:34,118
Are you his dad?

514
00:32:34,202 --> 00:32:36,663
You little brat! Talking back now?

515
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:39,582
[tense music playing]

516
00:32:46,631 --> 00:32:47,632
Sanggano.

517
00:32:48,132 --> 00:32:49,050
Yes, Congressman?

518
00:32:49,842 --> 00:32:54,055
Make sure everything is ready
before Miss Aguas and I enter.

519
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:55,765
Yes, Congressman.

520
00:32:57,934 --> 00:32:59,894
[tense music playing]

521
00:33:13,533 --> 00:33:14,659
Tell me the truth, Madrigal,

522
00:33:15,410 --> 00:33:16,953
so we can end this once and for all.

523
00:33:17,036 --> 00:33:19,080
And then what? You'll turn me
over to the Ardientes?

524
00:33:24,585 --> 00:33:26,462
I don't understand you! I'm on your side!

525
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:27,588
What's the problem?

526
00:33:28,089 --> 00:33:30,842
If this is the way my own group
and boss are going to treat me,

527
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:33,845
then I'll just leave.

528
00:33:35,638 --> 00:33:36,723
Madrigal!

529
00:33:36,806 --> 00:33:38,141
Come back here, Madrigal!

530
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:48,985
[thuds]

531
00:33:50,194 --> 00:33:54,115
[suspenseful music playing]

532
00:34:01,289 --> 00:34:03,791
[Julio] Surprise! Surprise!

533
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:04,876
[laughs]

534
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:08,671
Don't worry, Jaguar.

535
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:10,840
I am not here…

536
00:34:12,091 --> 00:34:13,593
for the carnage.

537
00:34:14,927 --> 00:34:16,429
If I can avoid it.

538
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:18,931
[Raul] Congressman.

539
00:34:19,766 --> 00:34:21,726
I thought you were busy with the campaign.

540
00:34:23,019 --> 00:34:24,228
But here you are.

541
00:34:24,312 --> 00:34:26,105
You still have time to visit me.

542
00:34:27,982 --> 00:34:30,485
Put your gun down
if you want me to believe you.

543
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:39,368
Ivy Aguas.

544
00:34:40,703 --> 00:34:43,081
I think this is our first time
meeting in person.

545
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,708
You truly are a beauty.

546
00:34:46,584 --> 00:34:48,377
May I please kiss your hand?

547
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:57,512
Don't come near me, Jaguar.

548
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:02,266
Where is Madrigal?

549
00:35:05,978 --> 00:35:07,230
He was here a while ago.

550
00:35:08,272 --> 00:35:09,357
But now, he's gone.

551
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:12,985
And, even if he were still here,

552
00:35:13,069 --> 00:35:15,988
I wouldn't just turn him over to you.

553
00:35:18,491 --> 00:35:19,492
Hmm.

554
00:35:21,327 --> 00:35:24,914
You uncouth weasel.

555
00:35:26,165 --> 00:35:27,166
Your man…

556
00:35:27,875 --> 00:35:30,795
used my gun to shoot Arnaldo.

557
00:35:31,546 --> 00:35:34,090
A gun that you stole from my armory.

558
00:35:35,424 --> 00:35:36,259
Now…

559
00:35:37,510 --> 00:35:39,512
for us to settle this nicely,

560
00:35:40,596 --> 00:35:43,099
give me Madrigal.

561
00:35:44,600 --> 00:35:45,601
Or else…

562
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:50,731
I'll blow this whole place up.

563
00:35:51,566 --> 00:35:53,776
And you know I'm capable of doing that.

564
00:35:54,318 --> 00:35:56,320
[Julio chuckling]

565
00:35:58,322 --> 00:36:02,034
[exhales] Congressman,
I think we already made our point.

566
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:06,080
It's possible Madrigal
might come back here,

567
00:36:06,164 --> 00:36:09,083
so if you kill Jaguar,

568
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,752
you won't be able to get what you want.

569
00:36:14,463 --> 00:36:15,506
[Julio] You know,

570
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:17,758
you're such a spoilsport.

571
00:36:20,094 --> 00:36:23,014
Jaguar, you are one lucky man.

572
00:36:23,931 --> 00:36:27,393
So lucky, because we have
a lady in our midst.

573
00:36:28,269 --> 00:36:29,270
Anyway,

574
00:36:30,313 --> 00:36:35,568
I'll give you 24 hours, no more, no less.

575
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:39,906
Give me Madrigal, or else,

576
00:36:40,948 --> 00:36:44,493
I will book you a one-way ticket to hell,

577
00:36:45,661 --> 00:36:48,414
with Satan as your bodyguard.

578
00:36:52,251 --> 00:36:53,169
[Julio] Oh, well.

579
00:36:56,672 --> 00:36:58,674
[tense music playing]

580
00:37:08,017 --> 00:37:09,060
Until next time.

581
00:37:31,582 --> 00:37:34,252
-[groaning]
-[shushes]

582
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:37,630
[Arthur] We're good people.

583
00:37:38,214 --> 00:37:39,298
We won't hurt you.

584
00:37:39,757 --> 00:37:41,133
Just cooperate, okay?

585
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:47,056
[muffled groan]

586
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:50,935
Here.

587
00:37:51,686 --> 00:37:53,187
Have some water.

588
00:37:54,272 --> 00:37:55,273
Go on.

589
00:38:00,444 --> 00:38:03,072
I said we were good people!
Weren't you listening?!

590
00:38:03,155 --> 00:38:04,907
-Let me go!
-Arthur, it's all right.

591
00:38:05,157 --> 00:38:06,158
I'll talk to her.

592
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:13,624
Diego Torillo!

593
00:38:15,626 --> 00:38:17,878
The Ardientes' bastard son.

594
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:20,548
What do you want from me, huh?!

595
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:21,966
Campaign money?!

596
00:38:22,508 --> 00:38:24,510
Well, you're not going
to get anything from me!

597
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:27,972
Divine Uytengco, I'll get
straight to the point.

598
00:38:28,931 --> 00:38:33,060
We brought you here to ask you
to be our whistleblower.

599
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:38,733
We have evidence of your corrupt
activities with Emilia Ardiente.

600
00:38:39,984 --> 00:38:41,068
Is this a joke?

601
00:38:41,610 --> 00:38:43,571
Emilia Ardiente is a friend…

602
00:38:44,238 --> 00:38:45,323
and family!

603
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:49,201
Well, if you don't cooperate,

604
00:38:50,077 --> 00:38:51,287
you're going to be in big trouble.

605
00:38:51,495 --> 00:38:53,414
And who the hell do you think you are?!

606
00:38:54,248 --> 00:38:56,375
Some ragtag hero for the poor?

607
00:38:57,877 --> 00:38:59,587
Emilia Ardiente is a dear friend,

608
00:38:59,670 --> 00:39:00,921
and she's on my side.

609
00:39:01,547 --> 00:39:02,923
And guess what?

610
00:39:03,299 --> 00:39:06,302
We're not scared of you, or anyone else!

611
00:39:07,261 --> 00:39:08,512
Who do you think you are, anyway?!

612
00:39:08,596 --> 00:39:09,930
Let me go!

613
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:12,600
I have places to go!

614
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:15,978
If I get out of here, you'll see!

615
00:39:17,313 --> 00:39:18,439
You'll see!

616
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:20,191
What do we do now?

617
00:39:20,816 --> 00:39:22,568
-You can't even do this right!
-If I were you…

618
00:39:23,402 --> 00:39:25,696
-I'd use force already.
-What? No.

619
00:39:25,780 --> 00:39:27,281
-Let me go!
-Trust me, Diego.

620
00:39:27,573 --> 00:39:28,741
I used to be a lawyer.

621
00:39:29,241 --> 00:39:32,244
And a case is way
more convincing with a witness.

622
00:39:32,828 --> 00:39:35,748
Arthur, if we force her,
she might just turn on us.

623
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:37,249
Just be a bit more patient.

624
00:39:38,209 --> 00:39:39,335
[Divine grunting]

625
00:39:39,418 --> 00:39:41,420
We need to get her to talk.

626
00:39:42,421 --> 00:39:45,966
And when we do,
Emilia will go down for sure.

627
00:39:47,510 --> 00:39:49,136
[Divine] I'll have my people
take care of you!

628
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:50,930
Let's be patient with her.

629
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:53,599
[Divine] What do you plan to do
to me anyway?!

630
00:39:54,809 --> 00:39:56,060
You can't do this to me.

631
00:39:56,852 --> 00:40:01,232
If you keep resisting, then
you'll never get out of here.

632
00:40:01,816 --> 00:40:03,901
[laughing]

633
00:40:03,984 --> 00:40:05,236
So amateur!

634
00:40:06,487 --> 00:40:07,947
Do you know what you're doing?

635
00:40:08,531 --> 00:40:10,699
Because it sure doesn't look like it!

636
00:40:10,783 --> 00:40:11,992
This is stupid!

637
00:40:14,870 --> 00:40:16,038
[Ivy] Julio will kill you!

638
00:40:16,122 --> 00:40:18,541
And Jaguar wants you dead
because his life is on the line!

639
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:21,127
Didn't you hear me, Ivy? I'm not leaving!

640
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:23,879
I'm the one who shot Arnaldo, remember?

641
00:40:23,963 --> 00:40:24,964
So, it should be me!

642
00:40:25,047 --> 00:40:26,090
Jepoy!

643
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:28,217
-Not you.
-Why?

644
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:31,095
You think I'll let him live
when he knows all my secrets?!

645
00:40:31,178 --> 00:40:33,180
No way in hell, Jepoy!

646
00:40:33,264 --> 00:40:36,267
I know you, Ivy. You're no murderer.

647
00:40:36,934 --> 00:40:38,185
So, what now?

648
00:40:38,936 --> 00:40:41,147
You'll surrender yourself
to the Ardientes? Really?!

649
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:42,648
If that's what I have to do, Ivy.

650
00:40:42,731 --> 00:40:44,567
There's no way I'm letting that happen!

651
00:40:45,943 --> 00:40:47,570
Listen to me, Jepoy.

652
00:40:48,696 --> 00:40:51,907
You won't surrender yourself
to the Ardientes.

653
00:40:57,329 --> 00:41:01,584
Enough! We've already gotten
so many people involved in this.

654
00:41:01,792 --> 00:41:03,836
Look at Aunt Camia and the others.

655
00:41:03,919 --> 00:41:05,171
They're all at the hospital!

656
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:07,256
Fighting is not going to help.

657
00:41:07,339 --> 00:41:10,509
We'll just end up wasting more time!

658
00:41:10,885 --> 00:41:14,096
Diego's right. Let's all talk
about this calmly.

659
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:15,931
Be on the same page.

660
00:41:16,932 --> 00:41:18,142
I know how you feel, Jepoy.

661
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:22,438
I know you're more than ready
to turn yourself over.

662
00:41:22,813 --> 00:41:27,693
But it'd be better if we worked
together to bring them down.

663
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:29,278
Especially Emilia.

664
00:41:30,988 --> 00:41:32,072
Jepoy, please.

665
00:41:33,365 --> 00:41:34,742
Listen to me.

666
00:41:43,918 --> 00:41:45,294
[phone ringing]

667
00:41:47,963 --> 00:41:48,964
[phone ringing]

668
00:41:52,134 --> 00:41:53,135
[phone ringing]

669
00:42:00,434 --> 00:42:01,435
Madrigal.

670
00:42:04,647 --> 00:42:05,773
Boss?

671
00:42:05,856 --> 00:42:08,734
That fake Jaguar is becoming…

672
00:42:09,235 --> 00:42:10,653
a real nuisance…

673
00:42:11,153 --> 00:42:12,321
<i>to our group.</i>

674
00:42:12,571 --> 00:42:16,283
Will you really abandon me now,
of all times?

675
00:42:18,494 --> 00:42:19,870
And one more thing, Madrigal.

676
00:42:21,372 --> 00:42:22,957
I apologize…

677
00:42:24,124 --> 00:42:25,167
for what I said earlier.

678
00:42:25,626 --> 00:42:26,627
I didn't mean it.

679
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:30,172
<i>The group needs you…</i>

680
00:42:30,839 --> 00:42:32,299
and you're the only one I can count on.

681
00:42:37,137 --> 00:42:38,138
Madrigal!

682
00:42:43,227 --> 00:42:44,228
Fine.

683
00:42:46,730 --> 00:42:48,691
I'll do what you want.
I'll keep my distance.

684
00:42:49,942 --> 00:42:51,652
Just make sure you keep your word.

685
00:42:52,361 --> 00:42:53,362
So, are we good?

686
00:43:32,234 --> 00:43:34,361
Luring your prey…

687
00:43:35,821 --> 00:43:37,406
so you can avenge your son?

688
00:43:38,365 --> 00:43:39,700
Or is it because…

689
00:43:40,200 --> 00:43:42,911
you really do need Madrigal?

690
00:43:45,748 --> 00:43:50,169
Who knows? Think of it
however you want, Natalie.

691
00:43:50,252 --> 00:43:52,963
I don't need to explain
myself to you. Got that?

692
00:43:53,213 --> 00:43:54,423
Well,

693
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:57,426
if I should take a wild guess…

694
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:02,640
It's for you to protect your son.

695
00:44:06,977 --> 00:44:10,648
Natalie, didn't you come back here…

696
00:44:11,106 --> 00:44:13,025
to avenge your father? Isn't that right?

697
00:44:14,276 --> 00:44:15,569
-Yes.
-Hmm.

698
00:44:16,028 --> 00:44:17,613
-Right.
-But…

699
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:20,908
unlike you,

700
00:44:22,159 --> 00:44:24,119
my revenge was worth it.

701
00:44:26,163 --> 00:44:27,748
My father loved me.

702
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:31,251
What about you?

703
00:44:32,378 --> 00:44:33,754
Does your son love you?

704
00:44:36,674 --> 00:44:38,926
Madrigal, on the other hand,

705
00:44:39,551 --> 00:44:41,220
we need him, obviously.

706
00:44:42,846 --> 00:44:44,890
Especially for our next heist.

707
00:44:46,016 --> 00:44:47,059
You know…

708
00:44:47,559 --> 00:44:49,770
we could earn millions from it.

709
00:44:50,562 --> 00:44:51,688
And I'm sure…

710
00:44:52,272 --> 00:44:55,192
it would be enough to compensate
for what Damian took from us.

711
00:44:56,485 --> 00:44:57,778
Do you catch my drift?

712
00:44:58,654 --> 00:45:01,073
We really need Madrigal.

713
00:45:02,324 --> 00:45:03,659
I'll let you decide.

714
00:45:03,909 --> 00:45:06,245
But make sure you choose
the right decision.

715
00:45:07,037 --> 00:45:11,375
Because if not, I'll take
matters into my own hands.

716
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:34,690
[soft music playing]

717
00:45:47,744 --> 00:45:48,745
Jepoy.

718
00:45:50,998 --> 00:45:54,793
You know, sometimes,
we think someone is meant for us

719
00:45:54,877 --> 00:45:58,964
because we share
something in common with them.

720
00:46:01,175 --> 00:46:04,386
We might think they're our soulmates.

721
00:46:07,431 --> 00:46:08,474
But they aren't.

722
00:46:10,017 --> 00:46:12,769
And that's the truth we need to accept.

723
00:46:24,406 --> 00:46:25,407
Anna.

724
00:46:26,450 --> 00:46:27,451
Listen to me.

725
00:46:28,619 --> 00:46:30,287
I'm leaving this place…

726
00:46:31,371 --> 00:46:33,624
so that you guys won't get
involved in my situation.

727
00:46:34,291 --> 00:46:36,835
Jepoy, didn't Lily tell you to stay here?

728
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:38,003
Where are you going?

729
00:46:38,712 --> 00:46:40,672
Somewhere far away.

730
00:46:48,847 --> 00:46:50,182
So I can protect you all.

731
00:46:52,935 --> 00:46:54,603
I'll return to the shadows.

732
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:23,090
[Ivy] <i>You can fight her</i>
<i>because she's just Emilia.</i>

733
00:47:23,173 --> 00:47:24,550
<i>And I am Ivy Aguas.</i>

734
00:47:24,633 --> 00:47:27,261
<i>If you agree to my plans,</i>
<i>Divine, we'll work together,</i>

735
00:47:27,344 --> 00:47:29,972
<i>and we'll bring Emilia down.</i>

736
00:47:30,055 --> 00:47:31,473
<i>Keep an eye on Raul's group.</i>

737
00:47:31,557 --> 00:47:33,183
<i>Find out if they're planning something.</i>

738
00:47:33,267 --> 00:47:35,769
<i>And just like what I did to Emilia,</i>

739
00:47:35,852 --> 00:47:37,020
<i>I will sabotage their plans.</i>

740
00:47:37,104 --> 00:47:38,355
[Raul] <i>This is all your fault!</i>

741
00:47:38,438 --> 00:47:41,149
<i>If not for you, the operation</i>
<i>would have succeeded!</i>

742
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:42,943
<i>-You did this on purpose, didn't you?!</i>
<i>-No, boss!</i>

743
00:47:43,026 --> 00:47:45,153
<i>Why would I do that?!</i>
<i>What did I ever do to you?</i>

744
00:47:45,237 --> 00:47:47,197
<i>To me? Nothing. But to my son? A lot.</i>

745
00:47:47,990 --> 00:47:49,741
[explosion]

746
00:47:51,034 --> 00:47:52,119
<i>Jepoy.</i>

747
00:47:53,328 --> 00:47:55,872
[theme music playing]
